  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN points on the number line, labeled 111 to NNN from left to right.\n\nChef is initially standing at point KKK.\n\nChef's goal is to reach point NNN. To do this, he can perform the following types of moves:\n\n\nMove one step left - that is, if he is currently at point XXX, he can move to point X−1X-1X−1.\nMove one step right - that is, if he is currently at point XXX, he can move to point X+1X+1X+1.\nMirror his position about the segment [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nThis means, if he is currently at point XXX, he will instantly move to point N+1−XN+1-XN+1−X.\nThe three types of moves can each be performed however many times he likes, and in any order.\n\nChef's position must lie in [1,N][1, N][1,N] at all times.\n\nFind the **minimum** number of moves needed for Chef to reach point NNN, starting at KKK.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input will contain two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum number of moves Chef needs to reach point NNN.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2101 \\leq T \\leq 2101≤T≤210",
      "1≤N≤201 \\leq N \\leq 201≤N≤20",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n10 6\n10 3\n7 1\n3 3",
        "output": "4\n3\n1\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef starts at K=6K = 6K=6 and wants to reach position N=10N = 10N=10.\nThe fastest way is to just move one step to the right four times.\nTest case 222: Chef starts at K=3K = 3K=3 and wants to reach position 101010.\nThis can be done in three moves, one method is as follows:\n\nMove one step left. Chef's position is now 222.\nMirror his position. Chef's position is now N−2+1=10−2+1=9N-2+1 = 10-2+1 = 9N−2+1=10−2+1=9.\nMove one step right. Chef's position is now 101010.\n\nTest case 333: Chef is at position 111.\nIf he mirrors his position, he will immediately end up at position NNN. So, the answer is 111.\nTest case 444: N=KN = KN=K, so Chef is already at his target position. No moves are needed."
      }
    ]
  },
